On a guess, from the error message, you are seeing a
file transfer protocol numeric error message "502",
which, it says here:

http://www.networksorcery.com/enp/protocol/ftp.htm

means "command not implemented". Either end of the
transfer could be causing the error, but more likely
the user end, or we'd see a lot more kvetching about
Hearse.

If that's a personal computer, you might have
typical overwritten and therefore corrupt software
due to operating system failures.

You might have noisy data lines that send mangled
messages to the Hearse server.

You might have a different version level of the FTP
standard implemented on your machine than on the
Hearse machine (unlikely as hell, FTP has been
stable for decades, I suspect).

You might have a buggy FTP implementation,
especially if you snagged a freeware one.

Somebody may have cast a serious hex on your
computer to take your mind off of NetHack. Does
your life include a neglected significant other?
If you have trouble remembering the answer to that
question, most likely it does.

Whatever, you need to isolate the cause, and most
likely fix it on your end.

